{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/950838-ananasi-kinfolk","id":950838,"title":"Ananasi Kinfolk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-14T18:40:57-07:00","id":950838,"title":"Ananasi Kinfolk","content":"Someone brought up the idea of the Ananasi in the Vampire forums earlier this week and it got me thinking that we do not know much about the Ananasi Kinfolk. Now, we know that the Ananasi reproduce with spiders and humans, but the animal Kinfolk are probably not that different than the local spiders (a smart spider is not that much different than a normal spider), but what of the human Kinfolk? Ananasi are unique among shapeshifters because they are the shapeshifter version of vampires so, in light of that, I am thinking about making the human Kinfolk of Ananasi the shapeshifter version of revenants.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that Ananasi Kinfolk would generate one blood pool per day, could store a maximum of ten blood pool, and could use their blood pool to heal as Ananasi and to fuel Gifts as Ananasi (they would be unable to spin webs, for obvious reasons). Unlike the revenants of Vampire, they would not be afflicted by the Beast because they are not creating a weak form of Vampire Vitae, so they would not be nascent psychopaths, but they would not age any slower than a normal human being. They would also not be available as a 4 point Merit, as their ability to generate and store blood pool would be too valuable, but I think that they could be balanced as a 8 point Merit for a non-Mage. I also think that they would be barred from becoming Mages, much as the revenants of vampire are barred from becoming Mages. I think it could be a fun thing to introduce, what do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:10:52-07:00","id":950851,"title":"","content":"Be careful A core theme of kinfolk (I agree its BS I know it I agree but still) Is their substantialy weaker then ghouls, its a problem I'd like to see fixed but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:14:17-07:00","id":950855,"title":"","content":"Is it a core theme or just a tendency? And does it necessarily apply to non-Garou Kinfolk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:26:05-07:00","id":950884,"title":"","content":"None of the themes of kinfolk have anything to do with ghouls. Kinfolk and Ghouls are not meant to be counterparts to each other from different games.<br /> <br /> For the OP, I don't think I understand the purpose behind having the Ananasi kinfolk be different from every other Fera's kinfok. If the idea is to just beef up kinfolk supernaturally, than you should come up with something across the board. Is there any reason that having dragonblood in your lineage should be less special than spider blood?<br /> And if you are playing up the Ananasi influence, then their kinfolk would in fact be &quot;nascent psychopaths&quot; just like the revenants. Ananasi are alienly cold and calculating. In the opening story a newly changed Ananasi eats her mother and moves on like it isn't a thing.<br /> <br /> Also...I'm curious where this idea that animal Kinfolk are smarter than normal came from. You've mentioned it a few times <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>, and I just want to know whether or not this is head canon or from the books. I'm not disagreeing by any mean, I just wanted to know where this came from.<br /> <br /> Apologies, as this post doesn't so much contribute as ask further questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:23:38-07:00","id":950905,"title":"","content":"I always figured they would be the weird kid that ate bugs for attention","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:53:57-07:00","id":950922,"title":"","content":"The animal kinfolk greater intelligence is implied in the sidebar on Wolf kinfolk in Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes. There is not technical maximum for Intelligence for Wolf Kinfolk, so I take it that the average Intelligence of animal Kinfolk is greater than that of normal animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}